On EBCDIC conversion-

I wrote a one-page COBOL program (quite an achievement in itself! :-)
which read EBCDIC and wrote ASCII; obviously only a minor mod is 
needed to do the reverse.

This was several years ago and I discarded the program; it was trivial 
anyway. Go through the COBOL reference manual. Off the top of my 
head I recall using statements like this:
...
SPECIAL-NAMES.
    ALPHABET EBBLES IS EBCDIC.
...
FD IN-FILE ...
    RECORDING MODE IS EBBLES.

And the PROCEDURE DIVISION was a simple READ then WRITE until end of 
file on input.

There's probably an even easier way to do it than this...

