This is my first response via NEWSRDR (was info-vax/mail) so I hope it goes
okay.  In some old article that I can't find, somebody asked:

> Hello - does anyone know if there's a way to format RD drives (RD53, RD54,
> etc) on a MicroVAX II using either VMS or a conversational boot setup?  

I've seen several replies indicating that it can be done either with Field
Service diagnostics or with a VAXstation 2000.  The only "reliable", "usable"
choice you have is to format it on the system type and controller type you
wish to use it on.  If you format the drive on a VAXstation 2000 it will not
be usable on the RQDXn controller.  I don't know the intimate details but I
went through this when moving an RD53 back and forth between a VAXstation 2000
and MicroVAX II.  Each time it was moved, it had to be reformatted on the
system.  The data is erased of course.

Seems to me a drive formatted on an RQDX2 can be used directly on an RQDX3 but
not vice versa.  I may be wrong on that one, somebody please provide a
non-flamer if not the case.
