Dr. Gokhale,

  Yes it's possible. Very possible. You can use a VT200, or equivalent,
for a console port off of tty0 on the second box. I'd recommend that you
connect the two of them over ethernet as you can then serve the second
box as a diskless client from the first. About the only item I would say
you should think about for the second box is a page/swap disk to be local.
But, how much you're ipacted by that will depend upon the types of data-sets
that you're doing your work on. In any case, you can get a fairly cheap
small disk for that and, I think, be very happy with the overall configuration.
The graphics display is the only functional variant between a DECstation
5000/200 and a DECsystem 5000/200.

  So, the minimum configuration is a VT type terminal and (optional) a page/
swap device.

