In article <hbo.701386085@sbphy.physics.ucsb.edu>, hbo@sbphy.physics.ucsb.edu (Howard B Owen) writes:
> 
>    Does anyone have the jumper settings for the above controller. I believe
> the designation is correct. It's a quad high QBUS board with M8639 and YB on
> the back. I want to try to run Ultrix 4.2 on my MicroVAX II, and my
> single RD53 is a little too small 8-).

  Sure. If you hold the board so the handle is up and the parts face you,
you'll see a row of 8 pairs of jumpers on the top, next to the LED's. These
set the starting unit for the controller. The right jumper is the 1 bit, and
the left jumper is the 128 bit. In sets the bit. So, if you inserted the
leftmost jumpers, you'd have DUx128:, where x is the controller number.

  There are then 11 pairs of jumpers on the bottom of the board, which move
from address bit 2 (A2) on the right to A12 on the left. The gaps represent
the spaces between octal digits. The default is IOIOOOIIOIO from left to
right, for 772150. 760334 is the common address for a second controller.

  Note that more than 1 RD-type disk isn't supported in a BA23 due to power
requirements.

