Well, seeing we are dealing with VMS: How about trying to call

    LIB$TRA_ASC_EBC(ASCII-SOURCE-STRING,EBCDIC-DESTINATION-STRING) ?

In that way you don't have to steal. You don't even have to think! (And, YES,
there is a LIB$TRA_EBC_ASC subroutine to do the reverse translation, and also a
generalized one, LIB$MOVTC, which will accept look-up tables of exotic versions
of the IBM encoding - especially the so-called Reversible Translation Table.)

