Not that it really matters...

The theoretical peak FLOP rate for the 21064 is one floating point
operation per cycle, making that 200 MFLOPS at 200 Mhz (or 150 MFLOPS
for the chips that are up for sale now). Of course, *peak* doesn't
tell you anything about *observed* performance (because by that
measure an 50Mhz i860 would have 100MFLOPS, if you could only find
code that does only multiply-add in an endless row :-).

The 21064 rate is for both double and single precision and would at
the same time allow for 200 million integer/load/branch instructions
to happen. Again, meaningless peak speed.


