this is how I went about it and you can modify it if you need to.
(I worked all TK50, I don't have the distribution on cdrom yet)

booted the tk50, when it asked for basic, advanced or system maintenence,
choose system maintenence.

look for a file called "INSTALL"  you may have to use "echo *" for directory
listings, I don't remember if "ls" is loaded at this point.  now using 
the only editor available "ed" edit the INSTALL shell script.  look for the
case statement which defines the RZxx drives.

when you locate this statement, put in another statement.  Ultrix will
probably identify your drive as a "RZxx" where all the other drives will
actually have a number.  you will need the actuall geometery of the drive.

there are two parameters you will need to install at this time, the 
parameter names are "ns" (Number of sectors per track) and "nt" (number of
tracks per cylinder).

ns should be self explanitory, however nt is actually the same as number of
heads, probably something like 15.

the above information will allow you to generate the root file system, and
ask you to reboot.  however I would recomend before you go any further,
edit the file "/etc/disktab"

this is when it would help to have another machine running ultrix, there is
a program supplied called "/etc/diskpart" run this with a "-d" option, 
supply all the parameters and you will get the proper output for the
/etc/disktab file. 

