On the other hand, one could say that crashme is the moral equivalent of
jabbing a screwdriver into the innards of your Walkman and then
complaining that it wasn't built sturdily enough.

I don't want to appear to be defending unrobustness -- certainly we're
working on hardening against the problems that crashme turns up and a
multiuser system does have to protect itself against malicious behavior.

On the other hand, system vendors have limited resources and have to
choose whether to spend them on things like defending against deliberate
attempts to tickle the hardware into failing or on things like adding
