One possible source of confusion on this topic is that the contents of the
diagnostics tape have changed over the years.

EARLY versions of the MicroVAX-II diagnostic tape could not be used to format
discs - you had to buy the "Field Service" kit which included a formatter. 
Actually, the customer tape did include the formatter, but access to it was
disabled. As it happens, in some revisions, the difference between the
Customer tape and the Field Service tape was precisely ONE BIT.

Later revisions of the diagnostic included a customer accessible disc
formatter. This happened at round about the same time as RD54 support was
added, though this is probably a coincidence. The customer formatter had a
somewhat different user interface from the old one - it didn't ask so many
questions which Joe User might find it hard to answer.

