There has been alot of talk recently about how magazines are now run
by advertisers resulting in a complete lack of coverage of GNU products
and other things of interest to customers. I talk to a friend about this
and we are thinking about starting a magazine but don't know if there is
enough of a market, or people willing to pay for a magazine that didn't
take large quantities of ad's.

For the following assume you where working for a company that did not
have net access:

1) Would you be willing to purchase a subscription only magazine?

2) Would you be willing to pay $5 an issue for a magazine inorder to get facts
   that where not biased by advertisers opinions?
 
3) What would you like to see such a magazine cover?

4) Are there any good unix magazines at all at this time?
