and/or SPECMARKs.  But there is rarely any information about the  I/O
characteristics of those machines, and in many ways these are at least as
important as the raw processing power.

In particular, I haven't seen any stats or numbers associated with the two I/O
elements of greatest importance on workstations: the SCSI bus(es) and the
Ethernet port.

How does the SCSI port and the Ethernet adapter on the various workstation
models compare to each other? For example, the SCSI bus on the VAXstation 3100
Models 30 and 38 are known to be very poor performers.  What about the  newer
VAXstation 3100 Model 76, and even better, what about the new VAXstation 4000
units?

What I basically would like is for someone to fill in the following table.  I'm
not sure what units to use for the SCSI bandwidth and Ethernet speed, but
probably just KB/sec would be enough to do comparisons.  (Note that the
Ethernet bandwidth is NOT 10MB/sec.  That is the theoretical capacity of the
Ethernet.  What I want to know is, on a completely unloaded Ethernet, how fast
can the VAXstation put data onto and take data off of the wire?)

