   In all, the UNISIG will present over 80 different sessions throughout the
symposium week. Topics specific to Digital's ULTRIX systems, the ACE
Initiative, the Open Software Foundation, as well as other types of UNIX
systems will be presented.

Topics of interest include:

* Real-life experiences with UNIX
* Descriptions of new technologies as they effect UNIX-based systems
* RISC-based systems, including RISC-based workstations
* Technical sessions on porting OSF/1 to new Digital architectures, such as
  Alpha
* UNIX-like systems, or UNIX-like tools on other operating systems
* VMS to UNIX migration strategies
* Tutorials on UNIX-based tools
* Programming techniques under UNIX-derived operating systems
* Windowing systems under UNIX and ULTRIX

   The week long format of a DECUS Symposium allows attendees to participate
in sessions ranging from their primary interest area to those offered in
related fields of interest. Forums such as SIG Campgrounds allow users to
meet other users in an informal atmosphere away from the classroom setting.

   DECUS Symposium attendees have the opportunity to solve their current
computing problems, learn new methods of dealing with everyday situations,
explore new applications and technological advances, and to make contact with
their peers in the computer industry.

