Lines: 22

In article <1992Mar17.223452.13924@athena.mit.edu>, ccount@boltzmann.mit.edu (Dr. Craig A. Counterman) writes:
> 
> Anyone ever see a case where a disk drive would fail such that
> a MicroVax II with three disks would not boot if that disk is connected,
> but would with it not connected?

  If the electronics on a drive fails, it could cause this. ST-506 interface
drives (which includes all of DEC's RDxx models) have a 34-pin common cable
and a 20-pin radial cable. If one of the signals on the common cable is being
interfered with, you can have all sorts of problems.

  It could also be the ready/write protect assembly in the BA123 front panel,
since that gets involved as well. Less likely are the M9058 signal distrib-
ution board in slot 13, or the RQDXn controller itself.

  This would also be a good time to mention that there is an FCO for RD53's
(only) in the BA123, which replaces the 50-pin ribbon cable between the RQDXn
and the M9058 with a shielded version.

