There would appear to be a small bug with the VT220
terminals I use.  This bug was not really evident until
I started poking around with an MNP modem.

It seems that when you have the VT220 set on "Smooth Scrolling",
it won't send Xon/Xoff when the buffer is full.  This happens
with 2400 baud modems as well, but to a lesser degree.  When the
MNP modem is communicating any higher than 2400 baud, and smooth
scrolling is enabled, characters, and sometimes whole blocks of
text are missed.  I've even tried using it with Modem Control,
but to no avail.  I haven't tested this theory with a data
line from the computer yet, but should that make a difference?

"Jump Scrolling" eliminates the problem entirely, but is
a little unsettling on the eyes.


Is this a recorded problem, or one that I have just uncovered?

If it is a known bug, is there firmware to correct the problem?

