  its DOS association in the minds of scientific/research consumers,
  where UNIX is said to reign.

  NT will have to prove itself in order to overcome this prejudice, and
  at this point, I doubt Microsoft will be able to pull of that kind of
  marketing miracle.  Further, Microsoft's technical abilities are, in
  the eyes of most UNIX people reading Usenet, dubious at best.

  Though I haven't considered switching from UNIX any time soon, I
  wonder just how many people are considering it, seriously.

  I wonder if the ACE members are getting many queries about NT, or if
  companies outside of the crumbling ACE consortium are loosing support
  contract renewals because of planned hardware/OS conversions toward
  NT.  I have to doubt it until I read otherwise.


