Here is my VMS VAXC version of the Unix "touch" program.  It can be used to
update/set the revision, creation, backup, or expiration dates of files
and comes with a full complement of VMS qualifiers (/LOG, /CREATE,
/BEFORE, /SINCE, /EXCLUDE) and a .HLP file.  Like Unix touch, it can
also be used to create a file if one does not exist.  It can be invoked
either by RUN, MCR, foreign command, or "native" command.  It compiles and
runs fine under VMS 5.4-3 and VAXC 3.1.

