The number one, _really_ original version of "RSX" (just that, no -11 part)
was developed and distributed for the PDP-15!  RSX stands for "Resource
Sharing eXecutive.  

When I was in grad school at the Univ. of Kansas we had a -15 that was used
for Earth resources satellite image processing research.  We mostly ran
PDP-15 DOS on it, but I also attended a DEC course on RSX because we
considered migrating to it.  I'm pretty sure that all of the RSX-11x
descended from there.  I may still even have an old manual at home some
place.  I do have a DOS reference card here in my office.
