Here at the University of Waterloo, we still have a fair array of uVAX's.
A number of our uVAX-II's are all still running straight 4.3BSD, while
we had to go to 4.3BSD tahoe for our two uVAX-III's (as the original 4.3
doesn't support III's I believe).  The uVAX-II's that we have later adopted
support on are still running Ultrix 3.x.  Ditto for a number of VAXstation
2000's - and we also have 2000's still running a locally modified Ultrix
2.x. The only machines we've ventured into Ultrix 4.1 and 4.2 are our
new MIPS based DEC hardware (5400's, 5500's etc.). The newer machines
have the necessary disk and memory to handle the vastness of Ultrix 4.x. 
But it has been a conscious decision not to go to 4.x on the uVAXen already
running 2.x or 3.x.


