  If the architecture of 1032 is similar to that of 1022 (e.g., "inverted file"
  indexes, files containing headers, indexes, and data together, etc) and if
  your database and applications are within reasonable "size" - e.g., no more 
  than a 100 tables or so, consuming 2 to 3 hundred MB max and relatively 
  simple joins - then I would say that the uVAX 3100 should work out fine as
  a replacement for the 6000/310 and the SCSI interface will do fine.  I assume
  you are using RA and/or DSSI disks connected directly to internal control-
  ler(s) currently (e.g., no HSC).  If so, I don't believe that you will see
  any real degradation in i/o. 


