We find it necessary to use ultrix disk quotas at our site.  Each user is
allocated a certain amount of disk blocks on the /u file system.  There is a
very serious bug with quotas on ultrix 4.2 in this setup.  I have seen
the same problem on earlier versions as well.  It seems that a write system
call will complete without an error indication even though the user is
out of allocated disk blocks.  This causes real trouble for programs like vi
which depend on the return status to know if it is all right to over write
the original file.  The most common situation, where this happens, is when a
user tries to write his file and leave vi when the user does not have enough
available blocks to hold the file.  Vi will think that the file was written
properly; but, the file is of 0 length.  Dec has stated that it is a problem
but can't say when or if it will be fixed.

Has anyone had this problem? and, if so, how did you get arround it?

Terry
