I am running a VAX 8700 with a DRB32-W on the BI bus. We are experiencing the 
following problem -

We have been experimenting with a test program and discovered that there seems to
be a  problem with the DRB. The interface on the VAX is sending unsolicited data to 
the user device connected to the DRB which confuses the user device. The sequence
of events go something like this -

        1) set up user device to send interrupt when trackball button is pressed

        2) set up ATTENTION AST on the DRB port (the ATTENTION AST seems to
           work as advertised)

        3) set up breakpoint in the AST routine to stop just after we enter the routine

        4) press trackball button

        5) two bytes of unsolicited data show up on the user device from the VAX

        6) stopped just inside the AST routine

        7) at this point any further commands sent to the user device are ignored
           since the user device is confused after getting the two bytes of
           unsolicited data

The two bytes of unsolicited data seem to be the second to last word (16 bits) of data
that were last officially sent to the user device from the DRB. It looks like we are seeing
output of a stale buffer when an interrupt is sent to the DRB port. This leads me to 
conclude that we have either a controller or a device driver problem. There are no
QIO's posted to the port at the time the two unsolicited bytes are sent, something
somewhere is causing the two bytes to be sent when they should not.

The user device in question is a METHEUS graphics controller. Has any one seen or
heard of similar problem? Know of any solutions? Any info would be greatly 
appreciated.

