Multi m-plus run no probs. Have run it on 70s, 73s, and 44s. The 44 also
had mp hooks in it. In fact some may remember that 4.1(?) of m ran like
a dog on 44s. Some one had set the cache by-pass bit for the kernal APRs...
And some where along the line the jumper that dissable cache bypass hit the
bit bucket. Come to think of it, the 44 was the only mach to have 2 valid
bit sets in the cache. Instead of haveing to wait for ALL cache locs to invalid
ate, you just switched to the other set.

> 
