 the 72 was a twin RSTS/E system with common disks. For runner to vax clusters,
little less functional. Don't think any shiped.

The 74s were real. Up to 4 CPUs, each with its own unibuss and up to 4 RH-70s
*EACH*. MKA-11 memory boxes. When canceled DEC had a load of them, so they
were re-designated 11/70-MU and used by AT&T and dec.
The CPU was a KB-11CM. It interlocked to ASRB instruction to memory for locking.

The not getting RSX to run on them is a load of crap. See you nearest M-PLUS
sources!

