Hi there...

Some background information.  We currently have 23 microVAX 3100's deployed
across Canada communicating via DECnet.  They are connected through
9600 baud leased lines to a hub connected to a VAX 6000/510 and VAX 4000.  

The next stage in our deployment is to connect 'remote sites' to each of
these microVAXes.  These remote sites would only have 3 terminals and a
local printer.  The remote sites are varying distances from a microVAX
(20 km to 1000 km).

Our questions:

1)  We are looking at two solutions for connection of the remote sites.  The
    first vendor is Motorola using the 6500 series of pads (X.25).  The
    second vendor is Micom using Marathon 5K and MB2's.
    If you can provide us with any insight to either of these solutions, or
    others please respond.  

2)  We have also encountered a response time problem when connecting 
    a microVAX to a DECrouter 150 to a DECrouter 250 to a DECrouter 250
    connected to Ethernet.  There are leased lines between each of the 
    connections.  With the DECrouter 150 in the above equation the 
    response time increases by about 25%.  Has anyone encountered a 
    similar problem or knows of a solution?

3)  Another challenge that is appearing is the monitoring of the network.
    With approximately 25 microVAX sites and 25 remote sites we need a
    comprehensive network management tool.  We need to be able to monitor
    DECnet, Ethernet, and LAT protocols.  Monitoring the DECnet and
    LAT protocols is where we are falling short.  Any insights would be
    greatly appreciated.


Please respond via email to any of the above questions.
I will summarize if there is enough interest or responses to warrant.

Thanks a lot,
Trevor.

