In article <1992Mar11.051239.15580@jrd.dec.com>, diamond@jit345.bad.jit.dec.com (Norman Diamond) writes:
> In article <630@wookie.dbaccess.com> steve@dbaccess.com (Steve Suttles) writes:
> >And for the record, the implementation on VAX C is definitely broken.
> I disagree.  My copy of K&R-1 doesn't have "assert" in the index.

Well, on my VAX C Run-Tim Library Reference Manual (AI-JP84A-TE, March 1987)
for VAX C Version 2.3, in section D-3 is written:

[...]
assert Macro
   #include assert
   void assert (int expression)
[...]

If then you look at the way assert() is defined:

# define assert(expr)                                   \
        if      (expr) ;                                \
        else { _assert ("expr", __FILE__, __LINE__); abort(); }

it's clear this is NOT a void expression. This is a statement.
