and keyboard.  You can connect a grayscale monitor to the BNC connector, or
you can connect an RGB monitor via a DB-something connector and a special 
DEC cable.  (sync on green)

Either way, the timing of the video is close enough to (U.S. broadcast tv)
standards that you can feed the grayscale output to a video monitor made for 
broadcast tv.  Or if you have such a monitor with RGB inputs, you can feed
them from the RGB signals.  

Anyway, if you have the color version of the VT240 (called the VT241, still
says "VT240" on the electronics box, but comes with an RGB monitor), you 
already *have* an RGB monitor.  Just disconnect the monitor from the terminal
and plug something else into it. 

