Ok, as promised, here is some information regarding the problems we experienced
when we installed our new RA72's.

Keep in mind that the errors only occurred on some of the drives.  After these
errors began to develop, Customer Service tried replacing the SDI cables and
some of the ECM's.  This did not stop the errors from occurring again, but it
did seem to delay their re-occurrence.  How or why is beyond anyone we talked
to.  The errors seemed to be always one of the following, and bear with me, I 
don't remember the exact words:

SDI Receive error
Lost read/write ready
Drive detected error, LED: 00
Lost receiver ready between sectors

I believe there were also pulse errors.

Our engineer said that problems have been encountered with RA71/72 drives that
are connected to K.SDI adapters.  Engineering has found that due to differences
in margin among several components on individual modules, errors can occur.
Specifically, pulse errors, some of which we saw, and I believe can cause
the other errors.  Everything was soft and correctable, so there was no concern
of data loss.

The problem was corrected with K.si adapters, but it is not recommended that
K.sdi adapters be replaced with K.si's, but there are some recommended minimum
etch/rev replacements if errors do occur with the RA71's and RA72's.  Remember,
these are only for problems with RA71 and RA72 drives being used with K.sdi:

Etch level D	Min rev C27	Latest rev C37
Etch level E	Min rev C28	Latest rev C38
Etch level F	Min rev C26	Latest rev C39
Etch level H	Min rev C36	Latest rev C40

Lotus was the first in the northeast region to have these problems, and for
whatever reasons were worked-out between our management and DEC Customer
Service, we replaced some of our older K.sdi adapters with K.si's, but this
will not be the recommended normal procedure.  (at least for now)

I have a question into our engineer as to whether there is a charge for
replacing the older rev adapters with the newer ones, when I find out, I 
will let you all know.

- kamal

