>I've been experiencing a strange problem with ``dxsession''
>going away on my DECstation 3100, Ultrix 4.2.

"going away"?  That's not very descriptive :-(

We had a problem at one stage with X sessions aborting and going back to xdm
(or Xprompter, depending on the machine) in the middle of people's sessions.

The eventual response from DEC was that it was a race-condition in Ultrix 4.2
causing the delivery of SIGPROF's to the wrong process.  When Xws gets one
it aborts.  We now have an Xws that traps SIGPROF, and a patched application
that no longer uses SIGPROF for its internal signalling, but I have not yet
seen a patch to Ultrix to fix the underlying problem.

It's conceiveable this might be affecting you, but from your description it's
hard to tell.

