I had problems with my session dying and returning to the XPrompter when
I'd open some appilcations.

I realized that the session died whenever I opened a task that had a fairly
large core image and had been swapped out.  I figured that Ultrix was
killing the largest task (which was almost always Xtm2d due to the bug that
causes it to eat core like there's no tomorrow).  I could be wrong about
the reason (in fact, I probably am) but I was still able to fix the problem
by changing some swap parameters in the kernel so that the minimum free
swap space was larger.   I haven't had a problem since.

