When I said I disagreed with the statement that the DECSYSTEM-20 was an 
improved DECsystem-10, I was talking about 2 levels:

1. The machines are physically identical. I booted up TOPS-20 on a blue 
box. There is no improvement from TOPS-10 to TOPS-20, other than it took 
until the 7.xx monitors for TOPS-10 to use KL paging on the KL-10 
hardware. The 6.xx monitors used microcode that made the KL processor do 
KI paging.

2. I felt then, and still feel, that TOPS-10 could compute circles around 
TOPS-20. TOPS-20 attempted to make a machine that simply wasn't that fast 
do some stuff that took some major computing and I/O, primarily paging 
against the system. I suppose TENEX and TOPS-20 were harbingers of the 
state-of-the art virtual systems to come, but when it came to practical 
computing during that era, it was simply faster to swap than page. It was 
a lean, mean operating system (that sure sounds hokey, doesn't it?)

As for the KS-10, that was indeed the 2020. It was pieced together from 
available parts, no special work at all. It had a Unibus, no RH20-style 
channels. Didn't matter, it didn't have cache, either.

BTW, for old DEC-10ers, did you see the posting from Queensland about 
their -10 going away? Don't forget to send your war/horror stories to them!

