Matt,

  A couple of suggestions for you:

	1. There have been revisions to the hardware you have. You probably
	   want, at least, a firmware upgrade.

	2. In the Ultrix v4.2a documentation set you will find a write-up on
	   writing TURBOchannel and VME device drivers.

	3. You can contact the TRI/ADD Program, triadd@pa.dec.com, for info
	   on the adapters.

	4. You can contact the EIC group that generated the DEC design. You
	   can reach them by sending mail to 	bruckman@solvit.enet.dec.com
	   which will put you in touch with Ron Bruckman who can help you with
	   device driver support for the DEC hardware (for hire).

Some things that I would like people to know about the Ultrix VME subsystem:

	1. TRI/ADD funds engineering efforts in USSG (Unix Systems & Software
	   Group) in order to have a common VME subsystem for all vendors. This
	   is true for Ultrix and will be true for the next release of OSF/1.

	2. The premise behind this is that all of the TRI/ADD vendors (and this
	   includes the DEC group, we treat them like anothe third party) that
	   are involved in TURBOchannel to VME adapters (this list currently
	   includes Design Analysis Associates, BIT3, VME Microsystems Inter-
	   national Incorporated and DEC/EIC) are given the same interface
	   documentation and technical support.

	3. If the groups choose to follow the interface of the subsystem, this
	   means that a VME device driver which runs on one adapter will run
	   on all of them. At the moment this is/will be true for three of the
	   vendors (VMIC has chosen to support Programmed I/O only and not DMA
	   at this point). I have been told by VME option vendors that porting
	   to our VME subsystem is no harder than porting to any other vendor's
	   VME interface.

  In any case, you can find more information and contact numbers for all of
the vendors involved in the TRI/ADD Shippable Products catalog which is on line
at   gatekeeper:  pub/DEC/TriAdd   for anonymous ftp.

  I hope that this information helps.

				Thanx,
