Has -fpe 1, 2 or 3 been useless?  DEC Fortran abides by a different set of
defaults for floating point exceptions.  For one thing, at certains settings
it forces underflows to zero and not do IEEE gradual underflow.  If MCNP
exceeds the range of floating point precision, then maybe -r8 will help by
using double precision instead of single precision.

The defaults we chose were, we hope, in line with helping users find numerical
problems with their code.

