Pardon me if this shows up twice, but it appears that my first posting did
not get off this site.

We have a 2400 baud V.42bis modem on a MicroVax II RS232 serial port.  The
modem wants to use CTS as hardware flow control, to tell the uVax when its 
buffer is full.  But the uVax just keeps on sending data anyway, even when
CTS is raised.  Thus people dialing in miss huge chunks out of their e-mail
or editor screen or whatever.

The only documentation we have for this serial hardware is a "DHV11
Technical Manual" dated 1983.  I can't find anything in there that gives me
any hope about being able to configure this (as a terminal port) to respect
CTS flow control.  Can anyone help me out with this?  We don't have much in
terms of $$, so upgrading our hardware is not a viable option just now. 
Are there any bits we can twiddle to make this work?  Advice would be much
appreciated.

