I'm afraid not.  There are no data sheets or users' guides, and the ISSCC
paper which describes NVAX is copyrighted by the IEEE, so I can't post it
or distribute it.  I can give you a few facts:

- Process: CMOS-4 (0.75u, 3.3V, 3 layer metal)
- Transistor count: 1.3 million
- Power dissipation: 18W worst case
- Frequency: 71Mhz, 83Mhz, 100Mhz
- Performance: 50 SPECmark89 at 100Mhz
- Translation buffer: 96 entry, fully associative, NMRU replacement
- On chip cache: 2kb Icache, virtual; 8kb combined I+Dcache, physical, two
  way set associative
- Off chip cache: 128kb to 2mb, direct mapped
- Pipeline: 10 stage macropipeline, like the VAX 9000

Hope this is useful

