The TF85's really do scream. If you do a MONITOR SCS on the machine doing the
backup, you will see the data rate going to the cartridge. This is only for
the DSSI version. If you have the machine to drive it (most can these days)
it will pump out > 700 Kb/s, which is great for this small drive.

CLD (shakey ground here) is sort of like an internal SPR. I think it stands for
Call Log Desk (or description) . Once a problem is found (SPR, CSC call) it gets
turned into a CLD, and it's rigorously tracked to resolution. Each call will
get turned into a CLD if it's a real problem.
