Alpha doesn't have "modes"; there is no "32-bit mode." It's a 64-bit machine
all the way through. The initial Alpha VMS will probably work with a 32-bit
address space, but the programs can run 64-bit data. Well, they will; all
you can really do with 32-bit data is get it into and off of the chip. Once
inside, it's all 64 bits.

