Apply the following UTTERLY AND TOTALLY UNSUPPORTED AND EVIL
patch to sys/fs/nfs/nfs_server.c (patch below).  This patch is
for Ultrix 4.2 source, but it is so simple that if your source
looks anything alike you should have no trouble adapting it.

At line 744 in /sys/fs/nfs/nfs_server.c (in the rfs_write routine) it
looks like this:

                                error = VOP_RDWR(vp, &uio, UIO_WRITE,
                                        IO_SYNC, u.u_cred);

change it to look like this:


                                error = VOP_RDWR(vp, &uio, UIO_WRITE,
                                        IO_ASYNC, u.u_cred);

and rebuild your kernel.  I cannot *currently* make a patched
nfs_server.o available as our nfs_server.c has other customizations
to add Kerberos security -- I will probably get around to building
a non-Kerberized version later this month, at which point I could
make it available via ftp (subject to DEC objecting?).

Remember, neither DEC nor I support this -- you're on your own.
It works for us, your mileage may vary.

John
PS,  Sorry, I can't make the Kerberized-NFS stuff available.
