	Hardware is needed to support a Nuclear Medicine computer system. This
system will be used for data acquisition, image display and image processing.
External CPUs may be required just for the analog data acquisition. The digital
signal can then be sent to the main computer. A description of the hardware 
requirements are given below. We are trying to find out what computer systems
can satisfy our system requirements.

1.   Display:  This is the most important aspect of our needs.  

     A.   Minimum we must be capable of displaying at the least and
          at the slowest four images (64 by 64 pixels) with an eight bit
          image display depth at the rate of 48 combined frames per
          second (equivalent of a 128 x 128 single image at 48
          frames per second).

     B.   Desired would be 256 x 256 or four 128 x 128's at 48
          frames per second of 256 gray scale

     C.   Display of static images should be capable of 512 x 512
          pixel images or larger (eg. 1024^2)

2.   Communication between CPU's should be no slower than Ethernet
     (10 megabaud) and newer faster communications (eg.
     Turbocharger) are desirable.

3.   Acquisition:  Capability should exceed 120 kbaud A/D
     conversion per card with adjustable digital conversion e.g. for
     32, 64, 128, 256, 512 square images or better eg. 1024, 2048
     or 726 x 512, 1024 x 512 etc.  Provision should be made for
     more than one card per system e.g. 5 or more cards max per
     system and for external stop, start triggering e.g. for gated
     acquisition and S.P.E.C.T.

4.   Storage should have read/write laser disk for archival and in
     excess of 400 Mbytes fast magnetic disk eg. 1 Gbyte.

5.   CPU(s) should be 32 bit (or 64 bit) with operating speeds at
     about 10 Vax units but no less than 3 Vax units.  (VaxStation
     4000 is 10 Vax units).

Thanks for any help - could any forthcoming replies be sent to me
directly at

	colin@femto.engr.mun.ca
--
Colin Au
colin@femto.engr.mun.ca
Memorial University of Newfoundland


