I get about 20 megapixels a second on my SPARC II in raw (pixrect) mode
and a good third of that under the more standard XWindows.  The latter is
300**2 images at 48 frames per second.  And SPARC II is considered slow
compared to what is announced for later this year.  The SPARC II is about
20-25 MIPS and many have announced 50-150 MIPS machines within a year.

Therefore I recommend do your software development on a general purpose
workstation for ease and portability.  You may be stretching their current
capabilities, but new ones will be more than adequate.  Thesoftware should
run on new ones without change.


