Arioch,

  I'd just like you to be aware that while there is fair chance that a
SCSI-2 Host can talk to a SCSI-1 Target (provided that the SCSI-1 Target
is ANSI SCSI-1 compliant with attention to the Common Command Set working
papers), there is a much smaller possibility that a SCSI-1 Host will be
able to successfully cope with a SCSI-2 Target (an overview of this was
provided in the second issue of Connecting, which is a regular newsletter
from the TRI/ADD Program, that you can have for free by calling or faxing  the 
Program office, numbers at the end of the post). I'm not saying that it's
impossible, just not probable. The SCSI-2 spec has addtional command structure
as well as values for a lot of items left undefined in SCSI-1.

  Just so you know. BTW, which DEC peripherals?

