Hello,
we have a network of Suns & DECs. Occasionally, we require to pass
integer/floating point data between these two machines & we are trying 
to locate a public domain utility/function to swap bytes for various data 
types (since the byte ordering of Suns & DECs is different). 

The tool `swab' swaps 2 byte integers but we require a 4 byte integer 
swapping routine. We are also trying to locate a similar routine
to swap floats (IEEE 754-1985 standard).

Does anyone know of such a routine? Has anyone written one (C, Unix 4.1.1)?

Thanks for your time,

Chris.


