Subject: HP to DEC DAT remote dump
Message-ID: <1992Mar2.211904.17493@newshub.ccs.yorku.ca>
Originator: jmuscat@nexus.yorku.ca
Sender: news@newshub.ccs.yorku.ca (USENET News System)
Organization: York University, Toronto, Canada
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 1992 21:19:04 GMT


We have a HP9000/380 running HPUX 8.0 in a multivendor LAN environment. We 
have been backing up our HP & Sun boxes remotely over ethernet to a DAT drive 
connected to a DecStation 5000/200 running Ultrix 4.2 using the dump command. 
The upgrade to Ultrix 4.2 is recent and we have noticed that our HP to Ultrix 
remote dumps have increased significantly in time. For example:


	File System 	Data Used	Ultrix 3.1    	Ultrix 4.2    
	Size				dump time	dump time
	-----------	---------	---------	---------

	900 Mb		400 Mb		28 min		8 hrs
	240 Mb		170 Mb		25 min		3.5 hrs
	
While the time has increased over 15 times in one case the number of tape
blocks used has stayed the same since the data used is approximately the
same. Our Sun boxes running both SunOS 4.1 & 4.1.1 have had no such problems
with the Ultrix 4.2 upgrade. 

Here is the dump command being run from the HP box:

   /etc/rdump 0udsf 250000 10000 - FS | remsh dumphost dd obs=10k of=/dev/nrmt0h

	(where FS is the filesytem being dumped eg. / or /users)

We could probabily live with the longer dump time but as is the dump times are
so long (ie an 8 hour ethernet connection to a remote device) that 4 out of 5 
times the HP dumps fail with the message:

	read: Connection reset by peer

Is there any fine tuning that can be done either on the HPUX or Ultrix side
to the the commands and/or daemons involved to reduce the dump time? The
other option would be to do incremental dumps but this is less convient than
full dumps.

